WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.190
"The rain set early in to-night,"
Wind tears at a lonely cottage.

2
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:08.100
Inside, a line is written with a quill.

3
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.270
Crossed out.

4
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.660
Written again, a little firmer.

5
00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:17.400
A calm voice begins to explain himself:
"Be sure I look'd up at her eyes".

6
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:22.360
When someone insists that hard,
should we trust him more, or less?

7
00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.430
In this mission, you'll
meet the dramatic monologue:

8
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.070
one character speaks, and
the poet is not the speaker.

9
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.360
You'll notice how he keeps
coming back to the same claim.

10
00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:35.650
And you'll hear how calm
and regular his voice stays,

11
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.640
line after line, beat after beat.

12
00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:41.980
Your mission: explain why
we shouldn't believe him.
